[gd_scene load_steps=6 format=3]

; HYBRID alphabet block -- D1's superellipsoid, re-proportioned around the
; lettering, in the house palette.
;
; The script is alphabet_block.gd, UNCHANGED. What changed is the type:
;
;   font_size 76 -> 83, and every Label3D lifted 0.0847 units.
;
; Both numbers were measured from Fredoka rather than chosen. Across a-z the
; glyph ink spans 0.894 em and sits OFF-CENTRE on the text origin, from +0.320
; em at the top of 'f' to -0.575 em at the bottom of 'y', because Label3D
; centres the line box (ascent + descent) and not the ink. On the shipping
; block that dropped every descender -- g j p q y -- 0.062 units below the
; plaque and onto the wooden frame.
;
; Lifting the label by 0.1275 em re-centres the ink on the plaque, and that is
; what pays for the bigger type: x-height goes 0.287 -> 0.313 units, 9% more,
; with 'f' and 'y' still clearing the edge by 0.023.

